  "_comment": "Voice recipe shared by pipeline/build_voice.py (baked story lines) and the mod's runtime TTS (AI replies), so both sound identical. Piper synthesises each sentence with length_scale = pitch * tempo, its melody is enlarged without changing speed or timbre (PSOLA, see 'prosody' and pipeline/voice_prosody.py), the audio is resampled by the steady 'pitch' (lowering the whole voice), and the line is run through a tiny effect chain. ringHz/ringDepth multiply the voice with a slow sine (a gargling, inhuman wobble); crush holds every Nth sample (digital grit). The everyday voices (ball, flat) use neither ring nor comb: on a voice whose pitch moves they make the timbre swim. 'intonation' is how strongly a profile follows the melody (0 = monotone).",
